i suggest you look more closely at this  no matter how many times we re-watch the  harry potter movies  there is always something new to  discover the filmmakers went above and  beyond when it came to hiding clues and  secrets within every scene  and all these years later we are still  uncovering some tiny yet incredibly  important details that have to be seen  to be believed  today we're checking out some of the  sneakiest hidden secrets from within all  of the harry potter movies  when harry first meets professor snape  snape asks him about a potion recipe  that we always assumed was a ploy to  make harry look bad in front of the  class  but actually it's so much more snape  asks harry  tell me what would i get if i added  powdered root of asparal to an infusion  of wormwood  if you don't know your victorian flowers  it's an easy message to miss  but it turns out that asphadel is  actually a lily  harry's mother and the victorian funeral  flower  and wormwood used to represent loss and  grief  after all this time always  harry first learns that his dad was a  talented quidditch captain and seeker  when hermione shows him a trophy with  his name on it in the hogwarts quidditch  trophy  case you never told me your father was a  seeker too  we almost missed another very important  name on the trophy right next to james  potter  none other than professor mcgonagall  herself  remember when neville gets a rememberall  in the mail a little magical device to  help him keep track of things  and yet i can't remember what i've  forgotten well if you look closely  neville is the only one not wearing his  robes  so we have a pretty good idea what he  needed to remember that day  did you know that the costume designers  used simple scarves to illustrate each  of the characters distinct personalities  ron's is slung carelessly around his  neck harry's is half on half off  and looks like he has been adjusting it  a lot and hermione's is perfectly and  neatly tied  of course you can also see it in their  ties how hermione's is done up properly  harry's is half undone and ron's is  almost completely off  there are so many details hidden in a  deleted scene from borgin and burke's in  the chamber of secrets  in it we see lucius and malfoy entering  the shop and they touch on quite a few  of the important items  we don't see what he is selling but  lucius takes care not to include  one unseen item in his sale that  particular item is not for sale  we later figured out that it was none  other than tom riddle's diary  that he wound up slipping to ginny in  the chamber of secrets  they used a super subtle lighting trick  in a really amazing way  when harry is first reading tom riddle's  diary before he gets pulled inside  he is lit with one candle that flickers  off of his face  once inside the diary everything  surrounding him is black and white  except for the same candle flicker  that's on him  while gilderoy lockhart had many wizards  and witches fooled  the filmmakers left a few little hints  lying around that if spotted  would make us wonder what exactly he was  hiding  one of those hints is definitely his wig  that's right right there on his desk is  a blonde wig  leading us to believe that even his  golden locks are a lie  you're a fraud you've just been taking  credit for what other wizards have done  the prisoner of azkaban is all about  time and no one knows more about time  than the legendary professor stephen  hawking  they wanted to pay tribute to him in the  movie so when harry is at the leaky  cauldron  he passes a wizard drinking a cup of tea  and reading none other than professor  hawking's book  itself a brief history of time  most of us if we were to encounter a  dragon  would be a little more worried for our  own safety than  it's the hungarian horned  but the filmmakers behind the goblet of  fire wanted to ensure  any animal lovers out there that even  mythical creatures were treated well  at the very end of the credits you can  see a disclaimer that states  no dragons were harmed in the making of  this movie  of all the subtle hints and clues hidden  in harry potter  sometimes it's clear that the designers  just wanted to have a little fun  which we noticed when we spotted the box  of cheery owls  that they stuck into the breakfast scene  in the great hall during the order of  the phoenix  looks like everyone enjoys cereal for  breakfast not just  muggles among the creepy skulls and  zombie hands in borgin and berks is one  more item that we wouldn't have paid  any attention to if it didn't come back  later in such a big way  except for the rapids do you understand  the cursed necklace that is accidentally  touched by katie bell in the half-blood  prince  is sitting on a bust inside one of the  dusty glass cases  lucky for harry he was ensnared by the  zombie hand instead  in the half blood prince we get to see  into dumbledore's memory of the first  time he met tom riddle  i'd like you to see it if you would and  in that moment  one sneaky clue tells us a lot about him  in the orphanage tom is standing next to  his window when dumbledore enters  laid out along the windowsill are seven  small rocks  which actually foreshadow his future  seven horcruxes  we often forget that lucius malfoy  actually spent some time in azkaban  after the events of the order of the  phoenix  but it's clear that he hasn't give me  the prophecy  now watch your friends  die in the deathly hallows part 2 in the  middle of the epic battle at hogwarts  when lucius reaches his arm out to his  son if you look closely  you can clearly see a tattoo of the  prisoner number that he was assigned in  azkaban written across his neck  there's one thing that muggles have over  wizards laser tattoo removal  a lot changes for the trio over the  course of the deathly hallows  but one subtle change for hermione let  us know subconsciously just how long  they had been hunting horcruxes for  if you watch closely you can see that  hermione's hair actually gets quite a  bit longer as the deathly hallows part 1  goes on  even when we thought snape had really  turned to the dark side  he was working for the order of the  phoenix the whole time  during his epic battle with professor  mcgonagall you can see him deflecting  her spells  right back at alecto and amicus the two  death eaters behind him  we may not have noticed at first but  he's actually protecting her in that  moment  during the deathly hallows part 2 right  before the battle of hogwarts  something professor slughorn did caught  our eye even though we never noticed it  before  right as all the hogwarts teachers are  making their way out of the school to  cast a protective spell  you can see slughorn taking a drink of  something in the background  it might be fire whiskey for courage but  some also think it could totally be  liquid luck  yes miss granger liquid luck  snape proved to be one of the bravest  characters in all of harry potter  during his last encounter with voldemort  snape is backed into a corner by nagini  though it's hard to tell because the  lighting is so dark if you look closely  you can see a gryffindor scarf hanging  on the wall next to him  symbolizing his bravery one of the best  reveals in all of the harry potter  movies is in the deathly hallows part 2  when we realized that voldemort hadn't  actually defeated the boy who lived  it's a triumphant moment for everyone  but if you look closely  it's also one of the most tragic when he  sees that harry is alive  george weasley looks over his shoulder  to where his brother should be  before realizing that fred isn't there  and will never be again  one more detail we never noticed is that  as harry ron and hermione slowly destroy  all of voldermort's horcruxes his robes  get progressively lighter and more faded  this was a subtle yet very effective way  to show that he himself is actually  fading away  the harry potter books and movies ended  in a much  much darker place than they began  literally  and figuratively and this transformation  is reflected in the entire tone of the  movies  including the opening titles the warner  brothers logo at the beginning of the  sorcerer's stone  is its usual bright cheerful gold but as  the movies go on it gets darker and  darker and darker with every year  and all of these are just barely  scratching the surface  if you caught any other hidden details  in the harry potter movies we would love  to hear about them  our favorite from this list is  definitely gilderoy lockhart's wig  thanks for watching
 

